# Resume fence — first-hop arming

When the operator message matches `^resume \d+`:

1. **First ULG hop:** `continuity(op=resume, thread=T)` where `T` is the thread id from the utterance. On `user-vortex-code` it is **overflow**: call `dispatch(tool="continuity", arguments='{"op":"resume","thread":"T"}')` (direct `continuity` ⇒ not found). Prefer not to `GetDynamicTools` / `tool_search` first — the hook **nudges** those bleed tools while `armed`, and never denies.
2. Pour is one `tape` call (or the inline bundle). `tape`, `get`, `cortex`, `rename_chat`, `retrieve`, and file reads stay **undenied**. If you receive an `rs_*` handle, `retrieve` it exactly once — it pops.
3. Cite ids from the returned `read_set.citable` when the bundle landed. Durable `agent_bus send` may carry the bundle's `fence_id` (from `fence.fence_id` or `fence_carriage.fence_id`); pass `transcript_id` on `continuity(op=resume)` when the tab id is known (FIX-15).

The IDE hook is a first-hop nudge, not a lock. `permission` is never `deny`. `sessionStart` drops the local marker so a Cursor restart unfences the tab. `checkpoint-discipline` pickup prose is guidance.

## Bundle pickup — verbatim before paraphrase

The hook stops at the pour; render order after it is this block. Read the bundle top-down **before** any
sketchboard, card, or prior-tab prose. Paths are bundle keys.

| Row | Source | Bind |
|---|---|---|
| 1 fence | `fence.fence_id` · `fence.state` · `fence.head_sha` | Read these to confirm the pour. `state=poured` (or the released terminal state) is the only "resumed" evidence. Speak `fence_id` and `head_sha` once, on the skippable receipts line after the picture. They do not open the reply |
| 2 tip + chain | `tip_checkpoint.turn_number` · `.body` · `.supersedes_turn` | Tip body **is** the mission — quote verbatim, never restate. Walk `supersedes_turn` back; a lower-numbered CP is superseded, not context |
| 3 highlight | `mission.highlight` | Quote as-is — the tip's own extract, not a seat summary |
| 4 summary_row | `mission.summary_row` · `resume_envelope.summary_row_source` · `.summary_row_as_of_turn` | Settled · live · next. `as_of_turn < tip.turn_number ⇒ label stale`; tip wins |
| 5 open line | `mission.resume_open` → `mission.open_line` | `open_line: null` is **normal** (card regex miss), not "no mission" — fall to `resume_open`, then row 2. Never fill the gap from a sketchboard |
| 6 secondary stale | `read_set.citable` ids with turn < tip | Sketchboard · log rows · earlier CPs are secondary: cite by id as `(superseded by #<tip>)`, ¬ paraphrase into Been→Are→Going |
| 7 handoff | `mission.handoff` · `mission.residue` · `mission.window_anchor` · `mission.bus_tail` · `mission.lifecycle.clone_mode` | `window_anchor` ⇒ Mode B + `scope=window` tape; fold `bus_tail`; `handoff` replaces external mission paste |

Read order in the fenced tab: this block, top-down, before any sketchboard, card, or prior-tab prose. A lower row does not outrank the tip.
Spoken reply: `operator-posture` Rule 3, which starts at the aim. This block does not open that reply. Fence id and head sha join the receipts line.
